  "published": "2026-10-30T11:30:56.137Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "9.2.3 - A type mapper built per call defined a dynamic assembly of its own, so a process that makes enough of them runs out of mappings for executable memory and fails with 'Failed to create RW mapping for RX memory' - a message naming insufficient memory and a Linux kernel limit, neither of which is the cause. This is the third level of the defect 9.2.1 and 9.2.2 fixed further down: both held the generator on the type mapper, so a caller who builds one per call never had one to reuse. Every type mapper now shares one generator, and the emitted entity factory is held per type, so twenty reads through twenty mappers define no dynamic assemblies where they defined twenty. It is a mitigation rather than a cure: a deserialiser and a serialiser are still emitted per mapper, so build the type mapper once and keep it - the README has a section on this. No API changes.",
